===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|seneschal|lang=enm}} (recorded in English since 1393), from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|senechal|lang=fro}}, from {{ML.}} (Frankish) {{term|siniscalcus|lang=la}}, from {{proto|Germanic|sini-|senior}} + {{proto|Germanic|skalk|servant}}; latter term as in {{term|marshal|lang=en}}.

Cognate to {{Fr.}} {{term|sénéchal|lang=fr}}.

